[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n3_osric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Osric at dusk, in the kitchen (night 3). The cellarer: short and heavy, round red face, always smiling; his ring of keys jingles.
# Jolly; he feeds you extra bread. (He started the killings. Nothing here says so.)
# Claims: n3_osric_page (lie): the cats get at the ledger. The cult tore the page (night 2); Osric handles the bodies.
== start
(Osric is at the kitchen fire, sleeves rolled, his ring of keys swinging at his belt. His face is red from the heat.)
Osric {glad}: The porter! Come in out of the cold. Mind the pot. You look half starved.
-> topics

== again
Osric {amused}: Back again? You can smell supper, can you. Not yet, porter. Not yet.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n3_osric_bread] What goes into the bread, Brother Osric? -> bread
* [if not n3_osric_supper] What's for supper, brother? -> supper
* [if not n3_osric_page] Has anyone been at my ledger, Brother Osric? -> page

== bread [set n3_osric_bread]
Osric {glad}: My bread? Rye from our own granary, baked in our own oven. Best in the ward.
Osric {glad, smile}: There's a bitter crust on it this week. The rye came in damp. It does no harm.
(He laughs, and claps you on the shoulder with a floury hand.)
Osric {glad}: I'll keep the heel back for you. A growing lad wants the heel.
-> topics

== supper [set n3_osric_supper]
Osric {glad}: Pease pottage, rye bread and small ale. Same as last night, and the night before.
Osric {amused}: Father Abbot looks to me like a man about to order a fast. Eat while you can, porter.
-> topics

# Asking the wrong brother the wrong question: Suspicion +5 (design doc).
== page [set n3_osric_page] [suspicion 5] [claim n3_osric_page lie]
Osric {glad}: Your ledger? Who'd want it? A list of wet pilgrims and their boots.
(He's still smiling. The knife in his hand has stopped.)
Osric {glad, smile}: Keep your cell door shut, porter. The cats get in. A cat will eat anything.
* [believe] I'll keep it shut, brother. -> page_believed
* [press] Cats, brother? I never said anything was gone. -> page_pressed
* [confront ledger_torn] A page is gone, brother. And a bed in the guesthouse stands empty that I wrote full. -> page_broken

== page_believed
Osric {glad}: Good lad. Now out of my kitchen, before you put your elbow in the pot.
-> topics

== page_pressed
Osric {amused}: (He laughs.) Didn't you? You've the face of a man who's lost something. Mind the pot, porter.
(He turns back to his fire.)
-> topics

== page_broken
(The smile goes out of his face. Then it's back, too wide.)
Osric {glad, smile}: Then your pilgrim got up early and went on his way, and took his page for a keepsake.
Osric {wary}: Count your beds, porter. I count loaves.
-> topics

== leave
Osric {glad}: Don't be late for supper! I'll keep the heel back for you.
"
